## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a compliant, scalable streaming pipeline with multi-region resilience, per-tenant isolation, and strong data governance.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region BigQuery with per-tenant isolation
- Dataflow transforms + DLP-based masking/tokenization
- Data Catalog for lineage and data contracts versioning
- 24h per-tenant rollback via snapshots
- Schema evolution handling and drift alerts

## Code Example
```javascript
// High-level pseudo orchestrator (conceptual only)
function flow(tenantId, event) {
  const masked = mask(event, tenantId);
  writeToBigQuery(masked, { tenant: tenantId, region: selectRegion(tenantId) });
  logLineage(tenantId, event, masked);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement schema evolution without breaking tenants?
- How would you test rollback correctness under peak load?

## Why This Is Asked
 Tests ability to design a scalable, multi-tenant privacy enforcement and incident response workflow on GCP, including data lineage, per-tenant isolation, and automated remediation under real-time load.

## Key Concepts
 - Real-time data processing, per-tenant isolation, data masking, DLP, Vertex AI, Dataflow, Pub/Sub, Data Catalog lineage
 - Event-time vs processing-time semantics, idempotency, backpressure, rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record){
  const r = { ...record };
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-****';
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{1})(.*)(@)/, '$1***$2$3');
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the anomaly model under bursty traffic and schema drift?
- How would you handle false positives/negatives and post-incident cleanup?
